--- !u!114 &1074965451
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1074965449}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Grab Points:\nPoses can be defined using the custom HVRHandPoser editor
    on each grab point. The grabbable object will be held in game as defined, choosing
    the closest pose if there are multiple.\n\nOne Hand Only: If true the grab point
    cannot be held by the second hand while in use.\nThe sledge hammer has been given
    two grab points each with this set to true.\n\nGroup: Grab Points selection is
    based on distance. Grab Points from the same group as the closest grab point
    will choose the hand pose with the closest rotation. The pistol slide has two
    grab points with the same group assigned.\n\nLeft Hand / Right Hand: Grab points
    can be limited to either the left or the right hand.\nThe clipboard has two grab
    points - one with left only and the other with right only\n\nHand Rotation Offset:
    The hand can be offset per grab point on any desired axis when held. The sword
    has a 40 degree rotation forward about the X axis.\n\nMaxDistance: Hand to Pose
    distance validation check, right most sledge hammer has this enabled and will
    fall back to dynamic posing if all grab points are out of range.\n\nGrab Point
    Swapper: Combat knife rotates between two poses.\n\tStandard Controller - A/X\n\tVive
    - Right Trackpad Down Click\n\tWMR - Left Hand (Trackpad Right), Right Hand (Trackpad
    Left)\n\n"
